From 77bede260e2c99097b1d2c3f147a14ab7ca3a522 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: malexander88 <malexander88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:00:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 1.0.2: Colouring plays Bach, Prelude in C (Kimiko Ishizaka,
 CC0) as a seamless -20 LUFS loop with a 12 s intro; the soft synth pad is
 removed; credits updated; APP_NAME constant for the coming rename

---
 public/CREDITS.txt             |  12 ++-
 public/audio/prelude-intro.ogg | Bin 0 -> 186283 bytes
 public/audio/prelude.ogg       | Bin 0 -> 2634135 bytes
 src/game/audio.ts              | 139 +++------------------------------
 src/game/credits.ts            |  15 +++-
 src/game/sim.ts                |  10 +--
 src/game/ui.tsx                |   6 +-
 7 files changed, 42 insertions(+), 140 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 public/audio/prelude-intro.ogg
 create mode 100644 public/audio/prelude.ogg

diff --git a/public/CREDITS.txt b/public/CREDITS.txt
index 87043dd..dd14a13 100644
--- a/public/CREDITS.txt
+++ b/public/CREDITS.txt
@@ -22,6 +22,11 @@ Träumerei (Schumann) — performed by Donald Betts; recording from Musopen (pub
 Source: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Robert_Schumann_-_scenes_from_childhood,_op._15_-_vii._dreaming.ogg
 Musopen: https://musopen.org/music/2326-kinderszenen-scenes-from-childhood-op-15/
 
+Colouring music:
+Prelude No. 1 in C major, BWV 846 (J.S. Bach) — performed by Kimiko Ishizaka,
+Open Well-Tempered Clavier. Recording dedicated to the public domain (CC0).
+Source: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kimiko_Ishizaka_-_Bach_-_Well-Tempered_Clavier,_Book_1_-_01_Prelude_No._1_in_C_major,_BWV_846.ogg
+
 Changes: each track was cut to a seamless loop (the Kevin MacLeod tracks with a
 1.5 s equal-power crossfade at a bar-aligned point), loudness-matched and
 re-encoded as Ogg Vorbis. "Daily Beetle" was cut to a 40-bar loop
@@ -32,6 +37,11 @@ start at once while the full loop loads.
 recording), looped with a 1.5 s equal-power crossfade (it is not a seamless loop),
 loudness-matched to -20 LUFS and re-encoded as Ogg Vorbis.
 
-Piano and Colouring: sounds and music made in the app.
+"Prelude in C" was trimmed of its leading silence (1.39 s to 155.1 s of the
+recording, ending as the last chord rings), looped by overlapping the final chord's
+2.2 s ring-out with the opening, loudness-matched to -20 LUFS and re-encoded as Ogg
+Vorbis. "prelude-intro" is the first 12 s of that same loop (as for every track).
+
+Piano: sounds made in the app.
 
 Open-source software notices: see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt.
diff --git a/public/audio/prelude-intro.ogg b/public/audio/prelude-intro.ogg
new file mode 100644
